    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_clean_endpoint_picard_multiplication_injectivity_reduction",
    "title": "Clean-endpoint Picard multiplication injectivity reduction",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact cohomology and relative bundle reduction",
    "statement": "The degree-one Picard section of a clean endpoint failure is exactly a nonzero kernel vector for multiplication by Q from H^1(O(N-rho,-T-m)) to H^1(O(N,-T)), of dimensions 60m^2+10m and 64m^2+4m. Relatively this is a fibrewise-surjective map O(N-rho)^(5m)->O(N)^(4m) with kernel bundle K_Q of rank m, degree m(5-4m), and a nonzero global section. All-negative splitting would logically close the branch, but the child elementary-modification theorem proves that strategy impossible and replaces it by an exact dichotomy.",
